# Work log (always)

After finishing any task, or stopping partway, **append** an entry to `WORKLOG.md` in the project root. Never skip this, even if the user did not ask. Do not wait to be reminded.

- Newest entries at the **bottom**.
- Keep entries short and factual. Write "not done" or "failed" honestly; never round up.
- Do not rewrite or delete older entries unless the user asks.
- `WORKLOG.md` is local-only (gitignored). Do not commit it.

## Entry format

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM IST · short task title
- Asked: one line on what I asked for
- Did: what you changed, in plain English
- Files: list of files changed
- Commits: hash and message, and whether pushed (and to which branch)
- Checks: typecheck, build and test results, pass/fail
- Database: which database you touched (dev / rehearsal / none), and confirm Production was not touched
- Open issues: anything unfinished, risky or needing my decision
```

Use the user's local time (IST). If unknown, use the timestamp from the conversation.

## Secrets

Never write secrets into `WORKLOG.md`: no connection strings, passwords, tokens, API keys, or full hostnames of production databases. Say "rehearsal database" or "dev database" instead.
